AI Surveillance Car Using ESP32-CAM 🚗

Project Overview

An IoT-based surveillance car developed using the ESP32-CAM module. The system allows users to remotely control the vehicle through Wi-Fi and view live video from its onboard camera using a mobile browser.

Key Features

- Wireless car control through Wi-Fi.
- Live video streaming using ESP32-CAM.
- Mobile browser-based camera access.
- Motor control using the L298N motor driver.
- Compact, portable surveillance vehicle.

Hardware Components

- ESP32-CAM (AI Thinker)
- OV2640 Camera
- L298N Motor Driver
- FTDI Programmer
- DC Gear Motors
- Wheels and Chassis
- 3.7V Li-ion Batteries
- 5V Buck Converter

Technologies Used

- Embedded C / Arduino IDE
- ESP32
- Wi-Fi Communication
- IoT
- Hardware Interfacing

Working Principle

The ESP32-CAM provides live camera streaming over Wi-Fi. The vehicle's motors are controlled through the L298N motor driver, allowing wireless movement. Users can access the camera stream through the ESP32-CAM's IP address using a mobile browser.

